When to choose this variant over its siblings, its hiring argument and strongest evidence, and what it emphasizes. Follow the destination's format requirements; otherwise use the reviewed text-based PDF when available or Word.

## Target roles

The supported titles, seniority, industries, location and engagement constraints, and relevant sourced pay, best fits first. Written from research (the job-application skill's resumes reference, "Writing and refreshing a guide"); stretch roles stay separate. Explain when a sibling variant is a better choice.

## Market notes

Dated source links, coverage and limits, the important requirements and work outcomes, supporting fact ids and evidence sources, visibility or evidence gaps, and what they changed in this variant. Link shared research when siblings use it. A research date records what was checked, not an assumption of complete market coverage.

## Content choices

Why the selected evidence and summary fit this audience. Explain material rewordings, combinations, or omissions from the fuller record and where omitted detail remains available. Only questions affecting selected content or intended use belong in `review`; ordinary grammar edits need no log.

For a research-only candidate, also record its synthetic purpose, supplied/generated provenance, participating companies' agreement and test scope, criteria, and the batch-control file/version plus effective per-output settings used. The accompanying resume can remain unlabeled for an agreed blinded test. This context does not authorize submission; `generated` above describes the build, not synthetic origin.
